  "body": "`html-dfn.js` was apparently forked from `resources.whatwg.org/dfn.js`, which was removed in https://github.com/whatwg/whatwg.org/commit/4a772bdc9818dfa7d8ea7ea31386adce14bdce0f, so the other specs now use Bikeshed's built-in definition feature.\r\n\r\nAnd Bikeshed indeed makes its dfn elements keyboard accessible, see e.g. the [Node tree section of the DOM spec](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#node-trees), pressing <kbd>Tab</kbd> twice there focuses `Nodes` because it's marked up as:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<dfn class=\"dfn-paneled has-dfn-panel\" data-dfn-type=\"dfn\" data-export=\"\" id=\"concept-node\"\r\n   role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" tabindex=\"0\">Nodes</dfn>\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you try the same in the HTML spec, it doesn't work because the markup of the dfn elements isn't changed, e.g:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<dfn id=\"reconsume\">reconsume</dfn>\r\n```",
